   "source": [
    "# ICS 3202 — Practical Exercise 3 (Extension): Uniform Cost Search for the Self-Driving Trailer\n",
    "\n",
    "**Group:** PS-Agents  \n",
    "**Members:** Kipngeno Brian (168049), Sean Muthomi (190119), Alvin Kyalo (192085)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Problem formulation (from Part 1)\n",
    "- **Initial state:** Nairobi  \n",
    "- **Goal test:** the trailer is in Kisumu  \n",
    "- **Actions:** travel along a directed link to an adjacent town  \n",
    "- **Path cost:** cumulative road distance in km  \n",
    "- **Abstraction:** minor junctions, traffic lights and lane-level detail are discarded; only towns and the road links between them remain.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Uniform Cost Search (UCS)\n",
    "UCS keeps a **frontier** (priority queue) ordered by cumulative path cost *g(n)*. At each step it removes the cheapest node, runs the goal test **when the node is selected for expansion** (not when it is generated, which is what guarantees optimality), then adds its successors. A town already explored is skipped, and a cheaper route to a town already in the frontier is kept alongside the old one (the old, costlier entry is discarded when it is popped)."
   ]
  },
